        "@id": "https://ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-9129-1",
        "name": "USN-9129-1",
        "description": "It was discovered that ZBar incorrectly handled certain QR codes, leading to a heap-based buffer overflow. If a user or automated system were tricked into scanning a specially crafted QR code, an attacker could possibly use this issue to obtain sensitive information or execute arbitrary code.",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2023-40889"
